WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:09.390
PRESENTER: In 1869, players
in the first football game

00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:11.640
used a round ball
like in soccer.

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:14.280
It was tough to carry
and awkward to throw,

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:17.190
so they changed it to look
more like a watermelon.

00:00:17.190 --> 00:00:19.170
The current shape
enables a better grip

00:00:19.170 --> 00:00:21.325
in passing on an arc
that's unique to football.

00:00:23.510 --> 00:00:29.760
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:32.009
A lot of people handle
a football before it

00:00:32.009 --> 00:00:33.750
ever gets to the field.

00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:35.520
They start with cowhide.

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:37.620
Footballs are traditionally
made of this leather

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:40.140
because it wears well over time.

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:42.960
With a die, a worker cuts
out the four sections

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:44.115
that make up the ball's skin.

00:00:49.590 --> 00:00:53.250
A stamping machine then brands
the skin with the company logo.

00:00:53.250 --> 00:00:55.840
They may put other markings
elsewhere on the ball

00:00:55.840 --> 00:00:57.780
depending on the design of
the model they're making.

00:01:04.170 --> 00:01:07.350
Each of the sections goes into
a machine that trims the pieces'

00:01:07.350 --> 00:01:08.880
combined weight down to spec.

00:01:16.660 --> 00:01:18.740
To strengthen the
skin, a seamstress

00:01:18.740 --> 00:01:27.290
sews cotton and vinyl linings
onto all four sections,

00:01:27.290 --> 00:01:29.840
then she places them in
a die that positions them

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:30.980
for another set of markings.

00:01:33.830 --> 00:01:36.380
These four white lines
will form two stripes when

00:01:36.380 --> 00:01:38.280
the sections come together.

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:40.550
This is purely aesthetic
and varies according

00:01:40.550 --> 00:01:41.570
to the football model.

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:45.710
Now it's time to sew the
top sections together

00:01:45.710 --> 00:01:48.140
and then the bottom
ones to each other.

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:50.150
Exactly how many
stitches this takes

00:01:50.150 --> 00:01:52.280
is this company's
closely guarded secret.

00:01:54.320 --> 00:01:56.750
This press makes a hole
in one of the top sections

00:01:56.750 --> 00:01:57.590
for the air valve.

00:02:02.060 --> 00:02:04.970
They make eight holes in
the top sections for laces

00:02:04.970 --> 00:02:07.589
that'll hold the skin tightly
around an inflated bag called

00:02:07.589 --> 00:02:08.389
a bladder.

00:02:11.090 --> 00:02:13.520
To join the ball's top
and bottom sections,

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:15.680
the seamstress first
cups them and then

00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:17.660
joins the edges together.

00:02:17.660 --> 00:02:19.730
She sews the leather
inside out to make

00:02:19.730 --> 00:02:21.980
the stitches less visible.

00:02:21.980 --> 00:02:24.080
Later, workers will
turn the skin right

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:27.320
side out by reaching through the
opening between the lace holes.

00:02:27.320 --> 00:02:29.480
This is also where they'll
insert the bladder.

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:35.840
It's important to
flatten the four seams.

00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:38.510
To do this, a worker
places each one on a wheel

00:02:38.510 --> 00:02:41.120
as a roller passes over the top.

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:43.730
This keeps the ball from
being bumpy when they stretch

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:44.990
the skin over the bladder.

00:02:49.730 --> 00:02:52.310
A 15-second steam
softens the leather

00:02:52.310 --> 00:02:54.450
and makes it easier
to manipulate.

00:02:56.750 --> 00:02:59.930
A concave press flattens
the seams at the tips.

00:02:59.930 --> 00:03:02.570
This will also keep the ball
smooth when they inflate it.

00:03:04.790 --> 00:03:07.010
Time to turn the
skin right side out.

00:03:07.010 --> 00:03:09.530
A worker places it
on a metal bar, then,

00:03:09.530 --> 00:03:11.900
reaching through the opening
between the lace holes,

00:03:11.900 --> 00:03:14.420
he grabs the other side of
the skin and pulls it through.

00:03:15.750 --> 00:03:18.890
Then he runs the bar along the
inside to reshape the skin.

00:03:23.570 --> 00:03:25.490
The bladder is made
of polyurethane,

00:03:25.490 --> 00:03:27.710
a type of plastic,
with a vinyl patch

00:03:27.710 --> 00:03:29.120
reinforcing the lacing area.

00:03:31.210 --> 00:03:33.730
After squeezing the
bladder inside the skin,

00:03:33.730 --> 00:03:35.860
a worker steps off the
end of the air valve

00:03:35.860 --> 00:03:36.970
to keep it out of the way.

00:03:39.890 --> 00:03:41.990
Then she inflates
the bladder a bit

00:03:41.990 --> 00:03:43.670
to make it rigid
enough for lacing.

00:03:45.750 --> 00:03:47.820
After setting the
ball with clamps,

00:03:47.820 --> 00:03:50.390
she uses an awl to thread
the lace through the holes.

00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:55.890
Just one vinyl lace
measuring four feet,

00:03:55.890 --> 00:03:58.680
it worms through both sides
and then down the center

00:03:58.680 --> 00:04:00.510
and through all the
holes once again.

00:04:04.590 --> 00:04:07.230
The lacing's spaced
about a half-inch apart--

00:04:07.230 --> 00:04:09.570
wide enough to comfortably
grip for that magic

00:04:09.570 --> 00:04:10.830
pass you've got in mind.

00:04:15.450 --> 00:04:18.314
Next, workers temporarily
over-inflate the balls.

00:04:19.560 --> 00:04:21.690
Steel molds surround
them to ensure they'll

00:04:21.690 --> 00:04:23.220
assume the correct shape.

00:04:23.220 --> 00:04:26.160
After 90 seconds, the
extra air seeps out.

00:04:27.760 --> 00:04:30.205
Finally, the factory
inspects the balls to ensure

00:04:30.205 --> 00:04:31.005
they're up to standard.

00:04:32.310 --> 00:04:35.850
Fully inflated, a ball must
weigh no more than 15 ounces.

00:04:38.430 --> 00:04:42.930
It should measure 21 and 1/2
inches through the middle

00:04:42.930 --> 00:04:45.210
and 28 inches around both ends.

00:04:50.070 --> 00:04:52.890
After a five-day
manufacturing process,

00:04:52.890 --> 00:04:56.030
these balls are
ready for the field.

